lands in the fleet repo. Every `Report:` trailer path below is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin - write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/<that path>.\n- Read-only on the lane; the ONLY writes are inside your own scratch dir /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r34-seats/<name>/ and your one report file. Never edit MANIFEST.json, the fleet templates/ or scripts/, .ufo/state/, .ufo/watchdog.log, any sibling repo, lane jj state or the lane Git index; never run git/jj write commands anywhere.\n- Tooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help the task - read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md first (official channels, update-safety gate, record tool/version/channel/reason in your report). pacman guard (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-20): all pacman transactions are PAUSED host-wide - install via `uv tool`/`npx`/an official binary in ~/.local/bin, or file an L0 question. Never `-Sy`/`-Syu`/`-U`/`-R`.\n- The kill rule is CONSUMED: do NOT run `python3 .ufo/evidence/round-33/c1/c1-measure.py --lane ... --rev ... --work ...` in default mode, ever. You MAY `import` the counter as a module in your scratch dir and call its functions (block_run, ho_witness_ok, run_tool_sandboxed, score_tool, public_panel) on scratch copies. Every command's exit code is captured with `cmd; echo $? > file`, never `&&`.\n- Your verdicts are observations: the deciding run stands; if you PROVE a landed artifact wrong, report it as a finding with reproducing commands - that is the wave's purpose.\n- Never `agent://all`; never pass a model parameter; routing is the operator's route table (~/.omp/agent/config.yml, read-only).\n",
