        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\n---\nname: godspeed\ndescription: >\n  Godspeed posture — name the axes, iterate cheap in parallel, keep moves that\n  improve any axis and harm none, and don't aim (let the frontier walk itself).\n  Stops clarifying questions and verbose planning in favor of large concurrent\n  tool-call batches. Use for any task framed with godspeed. Triggers: \"godspeed\",\n  \"--with godspeed\", \"/skill:godspeed\", or a task marked with godspeed framing.\n---\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\n# Target\nSetup: `mkdir -p /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r34-seats/Mutkillheadextraassign && env -u GIT_DIR -u GIT_WORK_TREE -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git clone -q --no-hardlinks /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r34-seats/Mutkillheadextraassign/lane && env -u GIT_DIR -u GIT_WORK_TREE -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git -C /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r34-seats/Mutkillheadextraassign/lane checkout -q --detach 0b99d48ed4e3d00c2e5893b2d61f3dd97a7f68b7`. All work in /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r34-seats/Mutkillheadextraassign/; the lane is read-only. Pinned bytes: `git -C .../lane show 0b99d48ed4e3d00c2e5893b2d61f3dd97a7f68b7:tools/tally-audit-v2.py > tool.py` and `git -C .../lane show 0b99d48ed4e3d00c2e5893b2d61f3dd97a7f68b7:tools/mutate-and-run.sh > pristine.sh`; verify sha256 against the pins above before any run. Verify against the TIP commit 0b99d48ed4e3d00c2e5893b2d61f3dd97a7f68b7 (the lane checkout is detached at it).\nAttack one sealed copy: `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-33/heldout/ho-kill-head-extra-assign.json`, labeled set=kill. (1) Re-derive the mutated runner bytes from pristine.sh with the JSON's edits (each old string exactly once). (2) Run the REAL tool on the copy via the counter's run_tool_sandboxed (import the counter from the lane path; scratch workdir) and record outcome/rc/last line - the label demands KILL (rc=1, TALLY_AUDIT: FAIL). (3) ADVERSARIAL: try to construct a variant of this copy (same fault family, different construction) that the amended ho_witness_ok VALIDATES but the tool labels opposite to its witness-set - or prove none exists for this family. If you find one, that is a critical finding; report the exact JSON.\n\n# Acceptance\n- Report: .ufo/waves/round-34/w1/Mutkillheadextraassign.md\n- Your report names the exact commands, exit codes and sha256s it relied on; every claim carries a pointer; a finding without a reproducing command does not count.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: operability, depth\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-34/w1/Mutkillheadextraassign.md"
